question_text:
Empty string default values are not displayed

If an option has a default value of `""`, the `show_default` option does not display anything. 

Reproducible example:
```
import click

@user.group()
def test_cli() -> None:
    pass 


@user_cli.command(help="Test CLI")
@user.option("--test_value", type=str, default="", show_default=True)
def test_function(
    test_value: str
) -> None:
    print(test_value)


@user.group()
def cli() -> None:
    pass


cli.add_command(test_cli)
cli()
```

Expected to see a default displayed. Actual behavior:
<img width="653" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/53453358/235223998-5e387b8b-45ac-41bd-af56-59ac177991fc.png">

Environment:

- Python version: 3.11.3
- Click version: 8.0.3

